WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.110
Most of us follow many newsletters, channels and boards, and read one or two.

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:08.410
The rest pile up unread, very patiently.

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:11.390
That's because each one is written for a crowd.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.810
It's like a buffet with a hundred dishes,

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:16.110
when all you care about is two dishes.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:23.250
So this time, you build your own personal newsletter, and pick its topics, sources and what to filter out.

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:30.690
And how often it arrives, how it looks, and where: Slack, email, or a Claude artifact for something more visual.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:37.950
Then its purpose: keeping you informed, or driving an action, for example finding features worth trying.

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:44.690
So in this adventure, you test the first edition by hand, then turn it into a skill and put it on a schedule.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:48.350
And once it has run a while, you improve it.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.110
Because the test is simple:

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:52.470
it's the one you actually read.
